Project Description
The aim of this project is to develop a full-stack web application based on the theme
“Sharing, exchange and building community”. The application is designed to support
cooperative sharing of resources, skills, or support between users for mutual benefit.
The project focuses on creating a database-driven platform where users can create
profiles, browse shared listings, and connect with other users. The backend of the
system is implemented using Node.js and Express.js, with MySQL used for persistent
data storage. Docker is used to provide a consistent development environment,
allowing all team members to run the application locally using the same configuration.
During Sprint 1, the focus of the group has been on project planning, repository setup,
and development environment configuration rather than implementing application
features.
Code of Conduct
All group members agree to follow the rules outlined below for the duration of the
project to ensure fair contribution, clear communication, and a professional working
environment.
Commitment to Tasks
Each member is responsible for completing the tasks assigned to them within the
agreed timeframe. Tasks will be assigned and tracked using the GitHub Project board.
All members are expected to actively contribute and make consistent progress.
Communication
Group members must always communicate respectfully and professionally. If a
member anticipates difficulty completing a task on time, they must inform the group in
advance and propose a revised plan or deadline.
Accountability
To maintain fairness and transparency, the group adopts the following accountability
process:
• First strike: An assigned task is not completed without prior communication. The
issue will be discussed within the group to clarify expectations and support
completion.
• Second strike: Repeated failure to complete tasks or communicate responsibly.
The issue will be recorded in the meeting notes and tasks may be reassigned if
necessary.
• Third strike: Continued lack of contribution. The matter will be escalated to the
module tutor, supported by evidence from GitHub commits, project boards, and
meeting records.
Fair Contribution
All members are expected to contribute a reasonable and balanced share of work.
Consistently missing deadlines or relying on others to complete assigned tasks is not
acceptable.
Respect and Professional Behaviour
All members must treat each other with respect. Disrespectful behaviour, including
dismissive communication, hostility, or undermining others, will not be tolerated. Any
disagreements should be addressed calmly and constructively.
Escalation
If issues cannot be resolved internally, the group reserves the right to escalate the
matter to the module team in accordance with module procedures.
Agreement
By signing below, group members confirm their commitment to this Code of Conduct.
