decisions in later sprints.
Ethical Issues
Several ethical considerations were identified during the planning stage of the project.
User data privacy is an important concern, and the application should only collect and
store information that is necessary for its functionality. User safety must also be
considered, particularly in relation to inappropriate behaviour or misuse of the platform.
Fair access is another key issue, ensuring that the application is inclusive and does not
disadvantage groups of users. As the project develops, suitable moderation and
reporting mechanisms will need to be considered.
Addressing these issues during Sprint 1 helps ensure ethical considerations are
embedded into the system design from an early stage.
